Package: aun-filestored
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Maintainer: John Brown <john@home-lan.co.uk>
Section: net
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/johnhomelan/aun-filestore
@DEPENDS@
Description: Econet (AUN) NetFS/NetPrint file server for BBC Micro and RISC OS
 aun-filestore is an Econet fileserver implementation (using AUN) for Linux,
 written in PHP. It provides file and print services to Acorn RISC machines and
 emulated BBC Micros on top of a layer 2 emulation of Econet, and includes a
 browser-based admin interface.
 .
 Ships init scripts for the main server (filestored) and the optional service
 providers (sharefsd, dnsd, ntpd, ecosyslogd, sql-serverd). postinst installs
 the procd (OpenWrt) or OpenRC (Alpine) variant into /etc/init.d/ depending on
 the running init system; none are enabled by default. Needs a PHP 8.4 CLI with
 the pcntl, sockets, pdo, gd, ldap, mbstring, xml, bcmath, zip and soap
 extensions.
